<!--
The blog listing, generated from each post's frontmatter rather than maintained
by hand: <RouteIndex/> lists this route's children, ordered by the number their
filenames carry and reversed so the newest reads first. A post's title,
description, author and date all come from its own `+++` block, so adding a post
is adding a file.

The `{ArticleMeta{..}}` spread is what frontmatter would be in a markdown page:
route metadata as a component, read off this file by the `<RoutesDir/>` scan (so
the nav knows this page before anyone visits it) and applied to the rendered page
as well (so the document title binds to it).
-->
<Fragment {ArticleMeta{title: "The Full Moon Harvest", sidebar: SidebarInfo{label: "Blog", order: 1, expanded: true}}}>
	<h1>The Full Moon Harvest</h1>
	<RouteIndex reverse="true"/>
</Fragment>
